// Louder Than Life 2026 — festival definition.
//
// Pure data: no schedule is built here. buildFestival() in shared/festival.js
// turns this into placed blocks, lanes and grid bounds.
//
// GENERATED by scripts/gen-greencopper-festival.py — edit the generator or
// regenerate rather than hand-patching, or the next refresh will clobber it.
//
// Source: the festival's own Greencopper app data, which is what
// https://louderthanlifefestival.com/schedule/ points people at (that page
// itself carries no times, only an app download link). The app's schedule
// JSON is served publicly:
//   https://goeventweb-static.greencopper.com/<project-hash>/<project-tag>/data/eng/shows.json
// with <project-hash> and <project-tag> read off the <goevent-web> element on
// the schedule page. Using it means these are the festival's exact published
// times rather than a transcription — and it is already fresher than the
// August press coverage, which still had Friday's Loudmouth closer as TBA.
//
// 197 sets across 7 stages and 4 days. Nothing crosses midnight (the latest
// end is 23:00), which the data model could not represent.
//
// Format per set: [stageId, 'HH:MM start', 'HH:MM end', 'Artist']
// All times are ET (24h).
